-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_optimize_defaults_missing.pcpp - pcpp: --defaults where the source gives no level

  A cli test: pcpp runs itself with the args (in the suite's output root,
  -o "$P:output" so the build lands there), on the fixture named; its
  output and exit code are the check. The source has no @optimize, so the default -opt fast applies: a
  release build, no heap report (without -opt it would be debug).
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_optimize_defaults_missing;

/*
  @@test
    kind cli
    args "--no-banner <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_plain.pcpp --defaults -opt fast -r -o $P:output"
    exitcode 0
    expect
    | Compiling <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_plain.pcpp
    | Target platform: x86_64-windows-gnu
    | Optimize level: fast
    | Subsystem: Console
    | Saving build file...
    | Building dir_cli_plain...
    | Build succeeded.
    | Output: <OUT>/bin/dir_cli_plain.exe
    | Running dir_cli_plain.exe...
    | dir_cli_plain runs
  @@end
*/

begin
end.
